Package: autoSpectra
Title: Soil Spectral Modeling, Visualization and Prediction
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Hugo",
    family = "Rodrigues",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "rodrigues.machado.hugo@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8070-8126"))
Description: An integrated platform for soil spectroscopy modeling,
    visualization, and prediction. Supports VisNIR (350-2500 nm) and MIR
    (600-4000 cm-1) spectra. Downloads and leverages the Open Soil
    Spectral Library (OSSL v1.2) to train two model families per spectral
    domain: a masked Variational Autoencoder (soilVAE) that is truly
    sensor-agnostic via spectral-dropout augmentation and per-mask SNV,
    and a Cubist + PCA(120) baseline that faithfully replicates the
    methodology of Safanelli et al. (2025, doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0296545).
    Both families use SNV preprocessing, log1p target transforms for skewed
    properties, 10-fold cross-validation with refitting, and applicability
    domain checks (Q-statistic for Cubist; Mahalanobis on latent space for
    soilVAE). Includes a Shiny interface for interactive prediction.
